{
  "Title": "ELSA-2026-500640: qemu-kvm security update (IMPORTANT)",
  "Description": "[7.2.0-44.el9]\n- scsi-disk: fix out-of-bound read in WRITE SAME (Paolo Bonzini) [Orabug: 40250898] {CVE-2026-81628}\n- hw/usb/hcd-xhci: More reentrancy guard fixes for the XHCI code (Thomas Huth) [Orabug: 40194860] {CVE-2026-111819}\n- hw/display/vga: fix OOB writes after external surface resize (Marc-Andre Lureau) [Orabug: 40188736] {CVE-2026-97889}\n- io: prevent unbounded read of websocket data from client (Daniel P. Berrange) [Orabug: 40188735] {CVE-2026-101291}\n- hw/usb/hcd-xhci: Set reentrancy guard in timer functions (CVE-2026-17588) (Thomas Huth) [Orabug: 40104739] {CVE-2026-17588}\n- hw/9pfs: mutate FID path from main thread only (CVE-2026-93834) (Christian Schoenebeck) [Orabug: 40104726] {CVE-2026-93834}\n- qga: Change effective user/group ID in guest-ssh-* commands (Kostiantyn Kostiuk) [Orabug: 40060417] {CVE-2026-12080}\n- virtio-balloon: fix free-page BH teardown on unrealize (Michael S. Tsirkin) [Orabug: 40060414] {CVE-2026-66899}\n- hw/net/virtio-net: strip trailing padding when caching RSC segment (Laurent Vivier) [Orabug: 40060413] {CVE-2026-66900}\n- io/channel-websock: do not lose QIO_CHANNEL_ERR_BLOCK while reading (Denis V. Lunev) [Orabug: 40060405] {CVE-2026-84788}\n- io/channel-websock: handle a blocked write during the handshake (Denis V. Lunev) [Orabug: 40060405] {CVE-2026-84788}\n- io/channel-websock: send an HTTP 400 when the greeting has no space (Denis V. Lunev) [Orabug: 40060405] {CVE-2026-84788}\n- io/channel-socket: do not treat a zero length write as an error (Denis V. Lunev) [Orabug: 40060405] {CVE-2026-84788}\n- hw/display/vga: fix text-mode OOB write after a graphics surface switch (Warisjeet Singh) [Orabug: 40039326] {CVE-2026-77913}\n- hw/virtio-rng: Fix host use-after-free (CVE-2026-50624) (Laurent Vivier) [Orabug: 39703366] {CVE-2026-50624}\n- virtio-pmem: wait for flush requests on unrealize (Michael S. Tsirkin) [Orabug: 39947075] {CVE-2026-63323}\n- virtio-mmio: fix QUEUE_NUM_MAX (Michael S. Tsirkin) [Orabug: 39825829] {CVE-2026-50626}\n- virtio-scsi: fix SCSIRequest leak on a bad request (Michael S. Tsirkin) [Orabug: 39903681] {CVE-2026-61476}\n- qemu-kvm.spec: Require matching QEMU common package for USB modules (Mark Kanda) [Orabug: 40120472]",
